          "source_text_sha256": "81179c3f85f1026b4c06b6eafd13bd771501c9ff9fafeba9168f755094b9510f",
          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: On March 25, 2021, at 10:15 PM, a witness is intrigued by the presence and movement of colored lights in the night sky. These lights form a large PAN triangle. A weak, muffled, and subdued noise is heard. Only one testimony is collected. The aeronautical context of the observation leaves no doubt about the explanation of the case (see the investigation report): - The witness was intrigued by the large size of PAN, as well as a noise and speed that he found curious. However, it must be known that an aircraft such as the CUJAS95 type A400M has a wingspan of over 42 meters for a length of 45 meters and a height of 15 meters.\n- The map of the National Center for Air Operations (CNOA) as well as the FlightAware site confirm the nature of the PAN observed that evening around 22:10/15.\n- Internet searches have allowed other witnesses to be found. The GEIPAN classifies this case as \"A\": mistaking it for a military aircraft, CUJAS95 type A400M.",
          "translation_text_sha256": "280d013112b5922f6c3378951956dc4e5c26afe965d89d1d1c239cc266e474ac"
        }
